<!-- Mask mode SUBTRACT: the left circle SOLID with the right circle bitten out of it, so the
     result reads as a cookie with a bite taken — JoyRaptor's own description, 2026-08-06, and
     literally what the shape does.

     The cookie is a shape no single pathData can express, so it is a clip-path group: clipped
     to the left circle, fill "the whole canvas EXCEPT the right circle" (evenOdd against a
     24x24 rect). An earlier version put evenOdd on the two circles alone, which also left the
     RIGHT crescent solid — that is EXCLUDE, not subtract, and it was wrong.

     The cutter is then restated as a DOTTED outline. VectorDrawable has no dash array, so the
     dots are 16 small filled circles placed around the cutter's circumference. -->
